a spirit airlines flight from las vegas  bound for pittsburgh had to turn around  just seconds before takeoff passengers  say they had to hold on tight as the  pilot slammed the brakes 8 news now  reporter victoria saha on this story  victoria  spirit flight 334 was supposed to take  off last night but right before takeoff  the faa says the pilots realized there  was something wrong with the air speed  indicator which made them push the  brakes  jennifer allen was on board with her  service dog on spirit flight 334 she  thought her tuesday night flight was  taking off like usual when they slammed  on the brakes obviously knew something  was very wrong you can see here from  flight radar 24 the flight was ready to  take off then stopped we were  full speed i mean seconds from lifting  off i actually thought we had  even begun to lift off spear airlines  released a statement saying the crew  decided to not take off due to a  potential maintenance issue the plane  braked safely upon taxing to the gate  the aircraft experienced a flat tire  we were sitting there on the runway we  heard a loud boom  and  the plane shifted weight  and we could see some sort of steam or  smoke out the window  the fire truck fire truck had come out  to the plane allen says the ordeal  continued passengers were left waiting  for hours after being promised a new  plane but it never came  she says it was it wasn't until 2 a.m  that she received a meal and a hotel  voucher the 9 40 p.m flight from last  night took off this morning close to 10  a.m reporting live from the newsroom  vitoria saha 8 news now
 

